{
  hvibe_version: "0.2.1",
  app: "z80-framebuffer",
  description: `a true instruction-level Z80 microprocessor emulator with full opcode execution, 64KB memory space, hex bytecode loading capability, and a 480x272 pixel screen bound directly to memory-mapped VRAM`,
  stack: [`javascript`, `html`, `css`],

  catalog: {
    globals: `
      const SCREEN_WIDTH = 480
      const SCREEN_HEIGHT = 272
      const BYTES_PER_ROW = 60
      const VRAM_SIZE = 16320
      const VRAM_START = 0xC000
      const VRAM_END = 0xFFBF
      const TOTAL_RAM = 65536

      const FLAG_CARRY = 0x01
      const FLAG_SUB = 0x02
      const FLAG_PARITY_OVERFLOW = 0x04
      const FLAG_HALF_CARRY = 0x10
      const FLAG_ZERO = 0x40
      const FLAG_SIGN = 0x80
    `,

    code: {
      square_move: `
        STRICT
        // Real Z80 machine code: 16x16 pixel square moving smoothly from left to right across the 480x272 screen
        // Bytecode sequence:
        31 00 FF AF 32 80 00 3A 80 00 5F 16 00 21 00 DE 19 06 10 3E FF 77 23 77 11 3B 00 19 10 F7 01 00 18 0B 78 B1 20 FB 3A 80 00 5F 16 00 21 00 DE 19 06 10 AF 77 23 77 11 3B 00 19 10 F7 3A 80 00 3C FE 3A 20 01 AF 32 80 00 C3 07 00
      `,

      vertical_scanlines: `
        STRICT
        // Real Z80 machine code: Full-screen alternating vertical raster scanlines (0xAA / 0x55) using hardware LDIR block copy
        // Bytecode sequence:
        31 00 FF 3E AA 32 00 C0 21 00 C0 11 01 C0 01 BF 3F ED B0 01 00 80 0B 78 78 B1 7A 20 F9 2F C3 05 00
      `,

      blinking_cursor: `
        STRICT
        // Real Z80 machine code: Realistic blinking text cursor (8x16 pixels) centered at 0xDE1E with hardware delay loops
        // Bytecode sequence:
        31 00 FF 21 1E DE 06 10 3E FF 77 11 3C 00 19 10 F9 01 00 80 0B 78 B1 20 FB 21 1E DE 06 10 AF 77 11 3C 00 19 10 F9 01 00 80 0B 78 B1 20 FB C3 03 00
      `
    },

    logic: {
      instruction_decode_execution: `
        STRICT ALGORITHM:
        The CPU executes raw Z80 binary machine code in a continuous Fetch-Decode-Execute cycle:
        1. Fetch byte at memory[PC] into IR, increment PC (modulo 65536).
        2. Decode and execute instruction according to standard Z80 opcode matrix:
           - Unprefixed opcodes (0x00 to 0xFF):
             * 8-bit loads: LD r, r' | LD r, n | LD r, (HL) | LD (HL), r | LD A, (nn) | LD (nn), A
             * 16-bit loads: LD rr, nn | LD SP, HL | PUSH rr | POP rr | LD (nn), HL | LD HL, (nn)
             * Arithmetic/Logic: ADD A, r | ADC A, r | SUB r | SBC A, r | AND r | XOR r | OR r | CP r
             * Increment/Decrement: INC r | DEC r | INC rr | DEC rr | INC (HL) | DEC (HL)
             * Jumps & Loops: JP nn | JP cc, nn | JR e | JR cc, e | DJNZ e | CALL nn | CALL cc, nn | RET | RET cc
             * Exchanges: EX DE, HL | EX AF, AF' | EXX
             * Miscellaneous: NOP | HALT | DAA | CPL | CCF | SCF
           - Prefixed opcodes:
             * 0xCB (Bit manipulation & shifts): RLC, RRC, RL, RR, SLA, SRA, SRL, BIT b, r, RES b, r, SET b, r
             * 0xED (Extended instructions): LDIR (block copy), LDDR, CPIR, 16-bit ADC/SBC, LD (nn), rr, LD rr, (nn)
             * 0xDD and 0xFD (Indexed operations): LD r, (IX+d), LD (IX+d), r, ADD IX, rr, INC/DEC IX/IY
        3. All memory read and write operations pass through the memory bus. Direct writes to addresses 0xC000..0xFFBF immediately mutate the video framebuffer.
      `,
      flag_calculations: `
        ALU operations MUST compute authentic Z80 status flags:
        - Sign (S): bit 7 of result.
        - Zero (Z): set to 1 if result is 0, else 0.
        - Half-Carry (H): carry out of bit 3 in 8-bit addition / borrow in subtraction.
        - Parity / Overflow (P/V): parity (even number of 1s) for logic ops, two's complement signed overflow for arithmetic.
        - Add/Subtract (N): 0 for addition, 1 for subtraction/comparisons.
        - Carry (C): carry out of bit 7 in 8-bit addition / borrow in subtraction.
      `,
      hex_bytecode_loader: `
        STRICT ALGORITHM:
        Parse a sequence of hexadecimal numbers (separated by spaces, commas, or newlines) representing assembled Z80 machine code.
        Write the parsed bytes sequentially into memory starting at target address (default 0x0000).
        Reset all CPU registers (A=0, F=0, B=0, C=0, D=0, E=0, H=0, L=0, SP=0xFF00, PC=0x0000) so the CPU executes the binary program from the entry point.
      `,
      framebuffer_blit: `
        Scanline-by-scanline direct memory blit:
        VRAM spans 16,320 bytes from address 0xC000 to 0xFFBF.
        For each of the 272 vertical rows:
          For each of the 60 bytes in the row:
            Read byte from memory[0xC000 + row * 60 + col].
            Map each bit (bit 7 down to bit 0) to corresponding canvas pixel (X = col * 8 + (7 - bit)):
              bit 1 => illuminated phosphor green (#39ff14) or crisp white (#ffffff).
              bit 0 => dark background (#0a0f0d).
        Canvas 2D ImageData buffer is refreshed every animation frame.
      `
    },
    tests: {
      instructionExecution: `GIVEN machine code bytes [0x3E, 0x42] (LD A, 0x42) at PC 0x0000, after one instruction step, register A MUST BE exactly 0x42 and PC MUST BE 0x0002`,
      directVramWrite:     `GIVEN machine code bytes [0x21, 0x00, 0xC0, 0x36, 0xFF] (LD HL, 0xC000; LD (HL), 0xFF) executed by the CPU, memory address 0xC000 MUST BE 0xFF and the first 8 pixels on canvas MUST BE illuminated`,
      loopInstruction:     `GIVEN machine code [0x06, 0x05, 0x10, 0xFE] (LD B, 5; loop: DJNZ loop), the CPU MUST decrement B down to 0 and loop 5 times before continuing`,
      blockTransferLdir:   `GIVEN instruction LDIR (0xED, 0xB0) with HL=0x0100, DE=0xC000, BC=16, 16 bytes MUST BE copied from source to VRAM destination and BC MUST reach 0`,
      hexProgramLoading:   `GIVEN a user provides a hex string '21 00 C0 3E FF 77', parser MUST write bytes [0x21, 0x00, 0xC0, 0x3E, 0xFF, 0x77] into memory at 0x0000 and reset PC to 0x0000`,
      squareMoveLocked:    `the generated code MUST load the exact bytecode sequence defined in catalog.code.square_move for the moving square program`,
      scanlinesLocked:     `the generated code MUST load the exact bytecode sequence defined in catalog.code.vertical_scanlines for the vertical scanlines program`,
      blinkingCursorLocked:`the generated code MUST load the exact bytecode sequence defined in catalog.code.blinking_cursor for the blinking cursor program`,
      canvasDimensions:    `the HTML canvas element MUST BE configured with width exactly 480 and height exactly 272`,
      vramSpan:            `VRAM MUST span exactly 16320 bytes from 0xC000 to 0xFFBF within the 64KB Z80 memory space`,
      playPauseToggle:     `GIVEN clicking the Play/Pause button, CPU execution MUST toggle between running and paused states`,
      standaloneBundle:    `the final output deliverable MUST BE a single self-contained HTML file without external libraries or assets`
    }
  },

  units: {
    output: {
      name: "Output Deliverable",
      features: {
        bundle: {
          description: `a single self-contained HTML file containing the complete Z80 instruction emulator, memory framebuffer blitter, hex program loader, and canvas interface`,
          inputs: [`code generation`],
          rules: {
            obligations: {
              self_contained: `MUST ALWAYS bundle all styling, Z80 instruction decoding engine, hex loader, and canvas rendering in a single standalone HTML document with zero external dependencies`
            }
          },
          tests: ["catalog.tests.standaloneBundle"]
        }
      }
    },

    cpu: {
      name: "Z80 Microprocessor Core",
      description: `authentic instruction-level Z80 emulation engine decoding and executing real machine code byte streams`,
      features: {
        registers: {
          description: `complete set of Z80 registers including main, alternate, index, stack, and program counters`,
          inputs: [`CPU reset`, `instruction execution`],
          rules: {
            obligations: {
              main_set:      `MUST implement 8-bit registers A, F, B, C, D, E, H, L accessible individually and as 16-bit pairs AF, BC, DE, HL`,
              alternate_set: `MUST implement alternate registers A', F', B', C', D', E', H', L' swapped via EX AF, AF' and EXX`,
              pointers:      `MUST implement 16-bit registers PC (Program Counter), SP (Stack Pointer), IX, and IY`,
              flags:         `MUST implement all Z80 flags in register F: Sign (S), Zero (Z), Half-Carry (H), Parity/Overflow (P/V), Add/Subtract (N), Carry (C)`
            },
            constraints: {
              reset_pc: `on reset, PC MUST BE initialized to 0x0000 and SP MUST BE initialized to 0xFF00`
            }
          }
        },

        memory_bus: {
          description: `64 KB addressable memory subsystem handling instruction fetch, data reads, and memory-mapped VRAM writes`,
          inputs: [`memory read from address`, `memory write to address`],
          rules: {
            obligations: {
              total_size:    `memory space MUST BE exactly 65536 bytes (addresses 0x0000 to 0xFFFF)`,
              vram_mapping:  `addresses 0xC000 through 0xFFBF (16320 bytes) MUST BE memory-mapped video RAM`,
              live_write:    `any Z80 store instruction (e.g. LD (HL), A, LD (DE), A, LDIR) writing to addresses >= 0xC000 MUST directly mutate VRAM`
            }
          },
          tests: [
            "catalog.tests.vramSpan",
            "catalog.tests.directVramWrite"
          ]
        },

        instruction_interpreter: {
          description: `true instruction decoder executing unprefixed opcodes (0x00-0xFF), CB-prefixed bit instructions, and ED-prefixed block/extended instructions`,
          inputs: [`CPU step cycle`],
          depends_on: [
            {
              feature: `registers`,
              when: [`fetching and updating register values`]
            },
            {
              feature: `memory_bus`,
              when: [`fetching opcodes and accessing operands in memory`]
            }
          ],
          rules: {
            obligations: {
              full_opcode_dispatch: `MUST decode and execute real Z80 binary opcodes: 8-bit/16-bit loads, arithmetic and logic (ADD, SUB, AND, OR, XOR, CP, INC, DEC), bit manipulations (CB prefix: BIT, SET, RES, shifts/rotations), block transfer (ED prefix: LDIR, LDDR), and control flow (JP, JR, CALL, RET, DJNZ)`,
              real_execution:       `MUST execute the actual binary bytecode stored in RAM starting at PC, updating CPU state strictly per instruction semantics without skipping or faking execution`
            }
          },
          tests: [
            "catalog.tests.instructionExecution",
            "catalog.tests.loopInstruction",
            "catalog.tests.blockTransferLdir"
          ],
          blueprints: [
            "catalog.logic.instruction_decode_execution",
            "catalog.logic.flag_calculations"
          ]
        }
      }
    },

    loader: {
      name: "Machine Code Loader",
      description: `subsystem for loading pre-assembled hex bytecode routines and custom user-provided Z80 machine code`,
      features: {
        hex_input: {
          description: `interactive input allowing the user to paste or enter hexadecimal Z80 machine code to execute directly on the CPU`,
          inputs: [`user pastes hex string`, `user selects preset demo program`],
          depends_on: [
            {
              feature: `memory_bus`,
              when: [`writing parsed machine code into RAM starting at 0x0000`]
            },
            {
              feature: `registers`,
              when: [`resetting PC to 0x0000`]
            }
          ],
          rules: {
            obligations: {
              hex_parsing:       `MUST parse whitespace-separated, comma-separated, or contiguous hexadecimal byte strings and write them directly into RAM at 0x0000`,
              built_in_programs: `MUST supply exactly the three pre-assembled Z80 programs from catalog.code: 1. Moving Square (catalog.code.square_move), 2. Vertical Scanlines (catalog.code.vertical_scanlines), 3. Blinking Cursor (catalog.code.blinking_cursor)`,
              reload_and_run:    `loading a program MUST clear VRAM, load the machine code at 0x0000, reset PC to 0x0000, and immediately start execution`
            },
            constraints: {
              exact_bytecode: `MUST NEVER replace or approximate the machine code of the three presets with high-level JavaScript shortcuts; the exact byte sequences from catalog.code MUST BE injected into memory`
            }
          },
          tests: [
            "catalog.tests.hexProgramLoading",
            "catalog.tests.squareMoveLocked",
            "catalog.tests.scanlinesLocked",
            "catalog.tests.blinkingCursorLocked"
          ],
          blueprints: [
            "catalog.code.square_move",
            "catalog.code.vertical_scanlines",
            "catalog.code.blinking_cursor",
            "catalog.logic.hex_bytecode_loader"
          ]
        }
      }
    },

    display: {
      name: "Direct Memory Framebuffer",
      description: `video subsystem continuously reflecting the 16,320-byte VRAM memory segment directly onto a 480x272 canvas`,
      features: {
        framebuffer: {
          description: `direct memory mapping translating 1-bit bitmap data from 0xC000-0xFFBF into 480x272 RGBA canvas pixels`,
          inputs: [`animation frame tick`],
          depends_on: [
            {
              feature: `memory_bus`,
              when: [`reading VRAM bytes at 0xC000 - 0xFFBF`]
            }
          ],
          rules: {
            obligations: {
              resolution:    `MUST render to a canvas with native resolution of exactly 480 horizontal pixels by 272 vertical pixels`,
              pixel_mapping: `each scanline of 480 pixels MUST read exactly 60 sequential bytes from VRAM, bit 7 to bit 0 for each byte`,
              retro_palette: `active bits MUST produce an illuminated phosphor green or white pixel, inactive bits MUST produce dark background`
            }
          },
          tests: [
            "catalog.tests.canvasDimensions",
            "catalog.tests.directVramWrite"
          ],
          blueprints: ["catalog.logic.framebuffer_blit"]
        }
      }
    },

    interface: {
      name: "Minimalist Interface",
      description: `clean retro display frame hosting the 480x272 canvas, playback controls, locked preset selector, and hex code input panel`,
      features: {
        screen_viewport: {
          description: `centered canvas element with crisp nearest-neighbor scaling and subtle retro monitor frame`,
          inputs: [`DOM render`],
          rules: {
            obligations: {
              canvas_element:  `MUST present an HTML5 canvas element with width 480 and height 272`,
              pixelated_style: `MUST use image-rendering: pixelated or crisp-edges to preserve sharp retro pixels`
            }
          },
          tests: ["catalog.tests.canvasDimensions"]
        },

        bottom_controls: {
          description: `a simple toolbar located beneath the screen with a program selector dropdown, a play/pause button, and a collapsible hex bytecode input modal or field`,
          inputs: [`user click on Play/Pause`, `user selects program from dropdown`, `user clicks Load Hex`],
          depends_on: [
            {
              feature: `instruction_interpreter`,
              when: [`toggling execution state`]
            },
            {
              feature: `hex_input`,
              when: [`submitting custom machine code`]
            }
          ],
          rules: {
            obligations: {
              play_pause_button: `MUST provide a single toggle button to play or pause CPU execution`,
              program_dropdown:  `MUST provide a dropdown selector with exactly three locked options: 1. Moving Square (Left to Right), 2. Vertical Scanlines, 3. Blinking Cursor`,
              custom_hex_modal:  `MUST provide an input area to paste raw Z80 hexadecimal opcodes, with a 'Load & Run' button that writes them to 0x0000 and starts the CPU`
            }
          },
          tests: ["catalog.tests.playPauseToggle"]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
